        "problem": "Solve the inequality\n\n$$\n(-1-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(|x|+2))(4x+7)\\le 0.\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "Since $-1-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(|x|+2)$ is always negative, we can divide both sides of the inequality by this quantity, but we have to remember to flip the sign of the inequality. By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(|x|+2))(4x+7) & \\le 0 \\\\ \\frac{(-1-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(|x|+2))(4x+7)}{(-1-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(|x|+2))} & \\ge \\frac{0}{(-1-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(|x|+2))} \\\\ 4x+7 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 4x & \\ge -7 \\\\ x & \\ge -\\frac{7}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
